1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,752
This Ruy Lopez line turns a pawn chain into a tactical net.

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:09,365
White and Black race to claim the center.

3
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:13,977
The bishop retreats, but the a and b pawns gain space.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:18,590
Black builds a chain that looks aggressive and secure.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,203
White challenges the center before the chain can lock.

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:27,815
The f pawn advances and opens the e file.

7
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,428
White jumps with the knight and targets the back rank.

8
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:37,040
Black captures in the center, trying to open an escape square.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,652
The knight takes on f seven and spots the rook on h eight.

10
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:46,265
Nxh eight wins the rook, while the passed pawn keeps running.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,877
The lesson: a pawn chain can trap your own pieces.

12
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:55,650
Would you see the rook trap in time?

